WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:12.290
The Council yesterday held its monthly meeting
for October, and early on the agenda was the

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.090
topic of speed limits in the Rangiora-Woodend
road area.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.340
Following community feedback, Council staff
are proposing that speed limits be reduced

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:26.680
along sections of Rangiora-Woodend Road, Gressons
Road, Boys Road &amp; Northbrook Road.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.869
Councillors approved public consultation on
the proposed changes, which is due to start

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:32.540
on the 8th of October.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.780
The Council also adopted the provisional Local
Alcohol Policy 2018.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.850
Changes from the previous policy attempt to
make rules around opening hours consistent

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.460
between on-licensed &amp; off-licensed premises.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.149
It also proposes that on-license opening hours
for the day proceeding a public holiday be

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:54.420
treated the same as weekends.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.120
The policy will return to the Council for
adoption once the appeal process is completed.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:06.580
Finally, the Council extended the District
Road Maintenance contract for one further year.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.580
The contract is currently awarded to Sicon.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.990
They have performed consistently well in quarterly
performance reviews, however some Councillors

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:17.560
expressed their desire to see a higher level
of service.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.909
Overall the district’s roading network is
judged as being in good condition and above

00:01:21.909 --> 00:01:24.080
average when compared nationally.

